  "limitations": [
    "Ordinary-input automated probes establish reproducible mechanics, not human enjoyment or difficulty.",
    "The broad matrix samples checkpoints 120/180/240 across configurations rather than testing all three for every configuration; these named runs separately match the legacy exploit at 210 and 240.",
    "The broad matrix couples seeds to encounter sets and airframes to configuration index; it is sampled coverage, not a full Cartesian sweep.",
    "A route that loses before its checkpoint has no mature unattended branch and must be reported as an early failure.",
    "No-input means no new movement, boost or Focus after the checkpoint. Inherited brief movement and automatic airframe replacement may still move the drone.",
    "Earned upgrade menus continue to be resolved on all branches, including after automatic replacement.",
    "These direct fixed-step probes do not measure rendered performance or host slow-resume wall time."
